<title>USA: AlliedSignal sets 2-for-1 stock split.</title>
<headline>AlliedSignal sets 2-for-1 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>MORRIS TOWNSHIP, N.J. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>AlliedSignal Inc said Wednesday that directors had approved a two-for-one stock split and a regular quarterly dividend of $0.26 per share on the pre-split shares.</p>
<p>The dividend, which is unchanged from June's payment, is payable September 10. record August 21.</p>
<p>The split is payable September 15, record August 21.</p>
<p>The shares are expected to begin trading at the post-split price on September 16.</p>
<p>Chief Executive Officer Lawrence Bossidy said the split was designed to make the share price more attractive for individual investors.</p>
<p>Since the company last split the stock two-for-one in March 1994, the share price has more than doubled, closing Tuesday at 91-3/16, the company said.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
